<title>USA: U.S. Coast Guard works to reopen Mississippi River.</title>
<headline>U.S. Coast Guard works to reopen Mississippi River.</headline>
<dateline>BATON ROUGE, La. 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tugboats are expected Thursday afternoon to attempt to refloat a freighter grounded near the mouth of the Mississippi River, a U.S. Coast Guard commander said.</p>
<p>Further upstream at Laplace, upriver from New Orleans, the Coast Guard also hopes to reopen another section of river shut overnight between mile 120 and mile 132 at midnight when 100 barges broke loose on the river, Coast Guard Commander Ken Parris said.</p>
